### 2. BGP Flow Specification Version 2 (FSv2)

* **FSv2 Basic IP Overview (`draft-ietf-idr-fsv2-ip-basic`)**
  * **Presentation:** Presented by Sue Hares ([04-FSv2 Basic IP Summary-v1](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-idr-03/materials/slides-interim-2026-idr-03-sessa-04-fsv2-basic-ip-summary-v1-00)).
  * **Discussion:** Summarized upcoming updates in versions -09 and -10. FSv2 utilizes a single NLRI with Unicast and VPN SAFIs. Key features include TLV component ordering, dependency filter chains, component flags (mandatory vs. optional/ignore), and validation rules. Keyur Patel noted that version 10 will define capability advertisement for filter families.

* **FSv2 Time Filters (`draft-zzd-idr-flowspec-scheduling`)**
  * **Presentation:** Presented by Li Zhang ([05-FSv2-Time filters zzd-idr-flowspec-scheduling](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-idr-03/materials/slides-interim-2026-idr-03-sessa-05-fsv2-time-filters-zzd-idr-flowspec-scheduling-01)).
  * **Discussion:** Defines a scheduling time component (type 200) under the time filter family. Based on feedback, the authors removed FSv1 extensions, eliminated a redundant priority field, and added clarifications regarding UTC clock synchronization assumptions.

* **FSv2 Bitwise IP Filters (`draft-kao-idr-bitwise-ip-filters`)**
  * **Presentation:** Presented by Nat Kao ([06-FSv2 Bitwise Filters draft-kao-idr-bitwise-ip-filters](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-idr-03/materials/slides-interim-2026-idr-03-sessa-06-fsv2-bitwise-filters-draft-kao-idr-bitwise-ip-filters-00)).
  * **Discussion:** Component types were renumbered to align with `draft-ietf-idr-fsv2-ip-basic` for IPv4/IPv6 source and destination payload bitwise matching.

* **FSv2 Packet Content Filter (`draft-cui-idr-content-filter`)**
  * **Presentation:** Presented by Yujia Gao ([07-FSv2-draft-cui-idr-content-filter](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-idr-03/materials/slides-interim-2026-idr-03-sessa-07-fsv2-draft-cui-idr-content-filter-00)).
  * **Discussion:** Defines component type 3000 to match static payload patterns in DDoS mitigation scenarios. Hardware testing on an ASIC demonstrated low latency overhead (~2 µs at 100 Gbps). Addressing comments from Robert Raszuk and Jie Dong, the presentation highlighted that this filter is meant for unencrypted, static patterns and requires explicit trust/import policy on eBGP boundaries.

* **FSv2 FlowSpec for QUIC (`draft-lin-idr-flowspec-quic`)**
  * **Presentation:** Presented by Yujia Gao ([08-FSv2-draft-lin-idr-flowspec-quic](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-idr-03/materials/slides-interim-2026-idr-03-sessa-08-fsv2-draft-lin-idr-flowspec-quic-00)).
  * **Discussion:** Defines components matching visible outer QUIC headers (Destination Connection ID, Source Connection ID, Header Flags) to allow traffic steering for QUIC sessions sharing common UDP ports.

* **Routing Filter Family (IP and AS/Community Filters)**
  * **Presentation:** Presented by Sue Hares ([09-IP and AS/community Filters for BGP Flow  Specification](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-idr-03/materials/slides-interim-2026-idr-03-sessa-09-ip-and-ascommunity-filters-for-bgp-flow-specification-01) and [09-FSv2-Routing-Filter-Family-Components](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-idr-03/materials/slides-interim-2026-idr-03-sessa-09-fsv2-routing-filter-family-components-00)).
  * **Discussion:** Explored filter components combining packet header matching with Loc-RIB route lookups to check Origin AS or Community attributes of the matching route.

* **FSv2 Actions: SRv6 Path Redirect, Redirect to Direct IP, and Traffic Compression**
  * **SRv6 Path Redirect (`draft-chen-idr-srv6-flowspec-path-redirect`):** Presented by Sue Hares ([10-draft-chen-idr-srv6-flowspec-path-redirect](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-idr-03/materials/slides-interim-2026-idr-03-sessa-10-draft-chen-idr-srv6-flowspec-path-redirect-00)), redirecting traffic to Binding SIDs or SRv6 SIDs.
  * **Redirect to Direct Connect IP (`draft-zhiwei-idr-redirect-ip`):** Presented by Zhiwei An ([12-FSv2-Redirect-to-Direct-ip Ext-Com Action](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-idr-03/materials/slides-interim-2026-idr-03-sessa-12-fsv2-redirect-to-direct-ip-ext-com-action-00)), introducing a Direct-link flag (D-bit) to invalidate redirect rules if the directly connected interface fails, preventing forwarding loops.
  * **Traffic Compression Action (`draft-shen-idr-flowspec-traffic-compression-action`):** Presented by Sue Hares ([13-draft-shen-idr-flowspec-traffic-compression-action](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-idr-03/materials/slides-interim-2026-idr-03-sessa-13-draft-shen-idr-flowspec-traffic-compression-action-00)), signaling RFC 3172 compression parameters. Joel Halpern noted on chat that encapsulation requirements associated with compression need to be clearly specified.

