### 3. BGP Base Specification Maintenance (`draft-ietf-idr-bgp4-rfc4271bis`)

* **Presentation:** Presented by John Scudder ([14-RFC4271bis Update](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-idr-03/materials/slides-interim-2026-idr-03-sessa-14-rfc4271bis-update-00)).
* **Key Topics:**
  * Re-emphasized scope: documenting existing mature protocol behavior to advance to Full Standard, rather than introducing new mechanisms.
  * **Version 03 Updates:** Fully integrated RFC 7606 revised error handling procedures. Added normative text allowing implementations to revert to session reset via configuration. Marked unreachable error subcodes as `deprecated`. Added a formal definition for "recognized".
  * **Open Question on NLRI Encodings:** John Scudder solicited WG input on how to handle legacy AFI/SAFI 1/1 encodings versus RFC 4760 (MP-BGP) encodings.
  * **Discussion:** Robert Raszuk, Jeffrey Haas, Keyur Patel, and Jie Dong discussed on chat whether RFC 4760 should be merged into the base specification or kept separate, noting tradeoffs between document complexity and reflecting modern implementation practices.

