### 4. BGP Best Path Next-Hop Selection Framework

* **Framework Introduction and Overview**
  * **Presentation:** Presented by Sue Hares ([15-18-19-Hares-BGP Best Path Selection Next Hop](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-idr-03/materials/slides-interim-2026-idr-03-sessa-15-18-19-hares-bgp-best-path-selection-next-hop-03)).
  * **Discussion:** Outlined how various next-hop documents (`draft-ietf-idr-bgp-bestpath-selection-criteria`, `draft-ietf-idr-bgp-bestpath-nh-selection`, `draft-ietf-idr-multinexthop-attribute`, SR policy drafts) relate to RFC 4271 tie-breaking rules.

* **BGP Best Path Next-Hop Selection Enhancements (`draft-ietf-idr-bgp-bestpath-nh-selection`)**
  * **Presentation:** Presented by Olivier Vroonen ([16-BGP Best Path Next-Hop Selection Enhancements](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-idr-03/materials/slides-interim-2026-idr-03-sessa-16-bgp-best-path-next-hop-selection-enhancements-00)).
  * **Discussion:** Addresses broken data planes and inconsistent metric comparisons across different transport types by introducing a Path Resolution Tuple (Resolution Key + Resolution Context) and Resolution Constraints / Preferences into the decision process. Kaliraj Vairavakkalai noted that resolution schemes (e.g., CT/CAR) can achieve similar functionality without making path preference changes mandatory. Jeffrey Haas highlighted three essential requirements: reachability check, convergence toward the egress exit, and consistent domain-wide forwarding to avoid loops.

* **BGP Next-next Hop Nodes (`draft-ietf-idr-next-next-hop-nodes`)**
  * **Presentation:** Presented by Kevin Wang ([17-Core-NH-draft-ietf-idr-next-nexthop-NHC](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-idr-03/materials/slides-interim-2026-idr-03-sessa-17-core-nh-draft-ietf-idr-next-nexthop-nhc-00)).
  * **Discussion:** Signals next-next hop nodes within the BGP Next Hop Capability (NHC) attribute to enable global load balancing (GLB) and offloading in CLOS fabrics. The draft was adopted and is undergoing revision based on directorate reviews.

* **MultiNexthop Attribute (`draft-ietf-idr-multinexthop-attribute`)**
  * **Discussion:** Sue Hares and Kaliraj Vairavakkalai reviewed how the multi-nexthop attribute specifies multiple next hops, tie-breaking criteria, and explicit forwarding actions (e.g., replicate, push, pop, swap), expanding traditional BGP next-hop semantics to broader forwarding paradigms.

