### 5. Core Adoptions

* **BGP Add-Path Limits (`21-Core-Adoption-Add-Path-limits`)**
  * **Presentation:** Presented by Donatas Abraitis ([21-Core-Adoption-Add-Path-limits](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-idr-03/materials/slides-interim-2026-idr-03-sessa-21-core-adoption-add-path-limits-00)).
  * **Discussion:** Signals a receiver's maximum desired paths per prefix using a new capability, and integrates a notification subcode when limits are exceeded. Kaliraj Vairavakkalai, Keyur Patel, and Robert Raszuk raised concerns regarding update group fragmentation and potential path oscillations when receivers specify different path limits.

* **Only-To-Customer (OTC) Route Server Verification (`22-Core-Adoption-OTC-RS-Verification`)**
  * **Presentation:** Presented by Antonis Chariton ([22-Core-Adoption-OTC-RS-Verification](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-idr-03/materials/slides-interim-2026-idr-03-sessa-22-core-adoption-otc-rs-verification-00)).
  * **Discussion:** Updates RFC 9234 procedure for route server clients to discard routes containing an OTC attribute if the AS in OTC does not match the route server AS, preventing route leaks across IXPs when route servers lack RFC 9234 implementation. The proposal received positive feedback on the list.

